# TEMPLATE — the ignore rules a repository owes before its first install.
#
# Copy these rules into your repository's own `.gitignore` and delete this
# header block. Your own rules — editors, language build products, whatever your
# work leaves behind — go beside them; these are only the ones the kits ask for.
#
# The install door refuses a dirty tree, so a file a door writes and no rule
# covers stops the NEXT install rather than this one.

# Machine-local harness settings. The shared settings file beside it IS tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Build directories. A kit that builds — the kennel does — writes under a
# `target/` inside its own tree, and every door of that kit refuses a repository
# carrying an untracked file, so a missing rule here stops the kit's own first
# build.
**/target/
